{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1501994-running-a-werewolf-the-apocalypse-game-set-after-the-apocalypse-need-ideas","id":1501994,"title":"running a werewolf the apocalypse game set after the apocalypse. need ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-02T19:29:33-08:00","id":1501994,"title":"running a werewolf the apocalypse game set after the apocalypse. need ideas","content":"OK so the idea is simple, the wyrm came to earth and actually was the red star (or the red star was a portal to Malfeas). This happened around 2000 to 2010. After it happened the forces of Gaia were able to defeat it and basically drove it off at great cost, over 90% of all the shifters (including Garou) as well as animals and humans were destroyed and the wyrm was only temporary defeated and driven back in return for the lives of the vast majority of every living thing that existed, including many incarna who were slain permanently.<br /> <br /> Now it is over 100 years later and society has moved into a neo-mediaeval era though there is technology in some isolated regions, thanks largely and part to vampires who still remember how to build stuff with simple materials, some of the leeches survived, and the wyrm has once again begun to encroach on the world and the present era is new dark age that is rising up to become a new civilization.<br /> <br /> The reason I'm doing this is because my players have no interest in doing this game in a historical era where they have to know any history and thus prefer that we are free to make up a new dark age style society since they don't want to play modern (too many limitations on behaviour around breaking the veil).<br /> <br /> Can anyone help me out with some ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T21:45:49-08:00","id":1502008,"title":"","content":"I recommend watching the anime Wolf's Rain. It has a lot of WtA themes, and is basically set in a post-apocalyptic world that is slowly dying, but still has some measure of civilization. You can probably steal a lot from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T23:08:55-08:00","id":1502009,"title":"","content":"There is also the book Apocalypse which details some post-apocalypse worlds to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T01:45:01-08:00","id":1502012,"title":"","content":"And every Apocalypse is something different. In our game we had the Apocalypse by saying, it whas the thing that the Nephandi worshiped that actually scared the weaver so much that in attampt to rescuing earth she tried to keep to everything safe by completely covering it so no influence can come in. Then when we freed the Wyrm and so healed his aching Gaia could spoke to her createres, that she send her choosen daughter to them who has the ability to turn every Kinfolk into a true breed because they will need the number for the upcomming fight. Then all the awakened, changeing breeds and even vampires -because Caine thought, I fucking hate god but where else should I live if this place is destroyed and so summoned all of his children there- where together with the Angels, their choosen hunters and the spirit of the dead they redied themself for the last battle.<br /> This last battle whas depending on perspective either a pyrrhic victory or heroic defeat. Because with 1% remaining they managed to survive and defeat/repell this Cthuluhuesque creater but her visions made it onto the earth. So now the whole planet is awakened and the only zones where magic is not random magic is in refugees but together with this awakener many new nephandi where created too. And so you have a planet full of people who think they could do better then you with now real option for reinforcement because you first need breed new Kinfolk and the newly awakened do not see the need for teachers because currently they could do just fine with trial and error.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T02:03:45-08:00","id":1502014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1501994-running-a-werewolf-the-apocalypse-game-set-after-the-apocalypse-need-ideas?p=1502009#post1502009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is also the book Apocalypse which details some post-apocalypse worlds to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>can you describe some of them. I don't own the book and I don't know if I want to buy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T02:12:32-08:00","id":1502015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1501994-running-a-werewolf-the-apocalypse-game-set-after-the-apocalypse-need-ideas?p=1502014#post1502014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> can you describe some of them. I don't own the book and I don't know if I want to buy it.</div> </div> </div> </div>My favourite whas, the wyrm suddenly has a moment of clarity, the true metis become his choosen champion and the Garou go united against the weaver instead to restore balance and the so freed Wyrm goes back to his original role of ending the sick and decaying so that the growth is not endless and so lead to a catastrophic mass decay.<br /> But on the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Apocalypse_(book)\" target=\"_blank\">wiki </a>the page has a description for every scenario.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":26160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","user":"Koronus","date":". 02-03-2023, 05:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T03:53:54-08:00","id":1502017,"title":"","content":"-Humans can rebuild pretty fast. Don't do a fallout 3/4, even New Vegas is too conservative. Things like bricks and a lot of other stuff are supprisingly easy to make and there are libraries everywhere, unless you're doing formori villages or some other cognative disadvantage the whole -everything's scrap metal and duct tape- vibe isn't going to work. Electronics might be difficult in some regions but but mechanical technologies will be recovered in a few years so long as there are people around and a safe network for building things. It's very hard to nuke people back to the stone age. By 100 years we'd have not only recovered but progressed again unless you add some extreme difficulties <br /> <br /> <br /> -Vampire bunkers/fortresses/prisons with humans as cattle... You're playing werewolf, might as well go full ham. <br /> <br /> -Go sci-fi and bring Hunter Spider spirits and other cool weaver spirits into the material world, perhaps possessing advanced robots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T14:49:40-08:00","id":1502050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1501994-running-a-werewolf-the-apocalypse-game-set-after-the-apocalypse-need-ideas?p=1502017#post1502017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Humans can rebuild pretty fast. Don't do a fallout 3/4, even New Vegas is too conservative. Things like bricks and a lot of other stuff are supprisingly easy to make and there are libraries everywhere, unless you're doing formori villages or some other cognative disadvantage the whole -everything's scrap metal and duct tape- vibe isn't going to work. Electronics might be difficult in some regions but but mechanical technologies will be recovered in a few years so long as there are people around and a safe network for building things. It's very hard to nuke people back to the stone age. By 100 years we'd have not only recovered but progressed again unless you add some extreme difficulties<br /> <br /> <br /> -Vampire bunkers/fortresses/prisons with humans as cattle... You're playing werewolf, might as well go full ham.<br /> <br /> -Go sci-fi and bring Hunter Spider spirits and other cool weaver spirits into the material world, perhaps possessing advanced robots.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree and I'm going in a completely different direction here. Basically once 90% of the population was wiped out in the initial first decade of conflict, a lot more people died of starvation. With the world totally warped and devastated the option to simply rebuild using knowledge out of books was just not there, the fact is there is not much of an opportunity to basically have the such advances in technology as that would require a huge number of people actually engaging in industrialization and suitable education and that's just not an opportunity for the survivors. <br /> <br /> The few pockets of civilization that survived were forced to go all the way back to meagre subsistence farmeing and totally dependended upon subsistence farming for food, as a result, once we run out of food we all die, once there is no supply chain we run out of food. That means everybody has to rely on making their own food and that becomes top priority number one as well as getting shelter. As such, the few pockets of civilization that exist are initially going to be entirely dependent on their ability to perform subsistence farming as there may be no trade at all and people are just as likely to kill you and take your stuff as they are to deal with your fairly.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, a lot of advance knowledge is absolutely useless in the hands of a single individual or even a group unless they have the formative knowledge to engage in the things those books cover (like engineering, metallurgy, medicine advanced beyond first aid). I've looked over books on chemistry metallurgy biology etc., they won't help me to build a factory and if we experience a catastrophic radical apocalypse over a very short period of time, my most pressing concern will be to get water, food and shelter so I live out the day or the week.<br /> <br /> Lastly, the presence of supernatural monsters roaming the planet openly, doesn't exactly encourage a very high likelihood of humans forming a cooperative educated and industrialized society with the necessary transportation and telecommunications required to support such a thing. No I could see many vampire run communes been quite successful in all of the aforementioned arenas, whether or not they would share their knowledge and power is another thing entirely though.<br /> <br /> That being said I really do want to point out that this is just my opinion and I am not an arrogant jerk, but I am willing to acknowledge that you might be right and I could be wrong, but I tend to think that an apocalypse would basically be a catastrophe and once the food chain runs out we are all going to die very quickly and that rebuilding society could easily take a century and that provides that we even have enough literature that didn't get used as kindling and toilet paper<br /> <br /> Oh and PS, I totally agree about fallout three and four. The fact that they even have old surviving buildings 200 years after the fall and that they are filled with Blamko macaroni and cheese, like the cardboard box its found in would not have dissolved after two centuries, strikes me as ridiculous. The fact that there are rolls of duct tape just laying around and that buildings are still even there aside from the rarest and most resilient strikes me as total bullshit. Even if you go with the RIFTS model where everything is mega damage capacity, you are still looking at a world where virtually everything that isn't MDC would be long gone and we either would have rebuilt or we would be in the Neo medieval.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T20:26:08-08:00","id":1502078,"title":"","content":"Another possible source of inspiration is the Hellboy comics, particularly the BPRD series of comics titled Hell on Earth, which is basically the Apocalypse and the end of the world. There were a lot of aspects of it that matched my own ideas of what the Apocalypse would be like (I admit that the scenarios in the Apocalypse sourcebook were far too tame for me. I envisioned a true &quot;The stars are right&quot; scenario of the Great Old Ones waking up again. The scenarios in that book seemed far too focused and too timid.). I think it did a good job of showing how modern human civilization would handle such an event, and how a &quot;post-human&quot; age of the world was being formed. Very terrifying. And while it may give little guidance to what a future post-Apocalypse world might look like, there is a lot you can pull from it as events that happened in your version of the Apocalypse and determine what the lasting after effects would be in your new setting.<br /> <br /> One aspect from that which I brought into my chronicles is that PENTEX is like the comic's Zinco Corporation. PENTEX became less about a group of people wanting to bring about the Apocalypse, and instead people who decided it was inevitable and were using it to allow them to survive it in the best possible manner. So you might want to consider some part of human industrial/technological civilization has survived - but it's basically the successor to PENTEX, and any humans in those areas have made their arrangements with what forces of the Wyrm they could and adapted accordingly. They could be a very sick and twisted remnant of humanity (or post-humanity) at odds with the other human survivors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T03:27:11-08:00","id":1502090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1501994-running-a-werewolf-the-apocalypse-game-set-after-the-apocalypse-need-ideas?p=1502050#post1502050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't agree and I'm going in a completely different direction here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that. Some more points for consideration.<br /> <br /> <br /> The people we now refer to affectionately as survival nuts will have a higher chance of surviving whatever it is and spreading their knowledge.<br /> <br /> If there really is a lot of monster threats on the planet, everyone's going to b-line towards producing firearms. Firearms aren't a high technology, they're something average people can manufacture in a garage and the supply lines/materials needed are very easy to acquire. Guns&gt;Monsters, so unless someone's spamming Jam Technology people will be commonly using fully automatic assault rifles with modern materials and cannons by 100 years.<br /> <br /> <br /> Something like 38% of the planet's land is estimated to be farmland. Yes, I suppose some wyrm plagues could make reclamation difficult. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think you're underestimating how much people could do pre-industrialization, and a good chunk of innovations were really having the idea to do something rather than dependent on technology. Say, getting to 7mm nano processors is extremely difficult, but using flintlocks rather than matchlocks? easy. Especially if we have examples rusting around to give us guidance. People are pretty resourceful and good at reverse engineering things. If we really got post apocalypted with many dangers around, I'd expect Castles and Guns to be widespread before 10 years, and something like WWII civilization before a hundred years. Some areas could be very lacking; ship building very far removed from how it's done today and how it's done today would be difficult to start doing in this new world.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T13:53:05-08:00","id":1502138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1501994-running-a-werewolf-the-apocalypse-game-set-after-the-apocalypse-need-ideas?p=1502090#post1502090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand that. Some more points for consideration.<br /> <br /> <br /> The people we now refer to affectionately as survival nuts will have a higher chance of surviving whatever it is and spreading their knowledge.<br /> <br /> If there really is a lot of monster threats on the planet, everyone's going to b-line towards producing firearms. Firearms aren't a high technology, they're something average people can manufacture in a garage and the supply lines/materials needed are very easy to acquire. Guns&gt;Monsters, so unless someone's spamming Jam Technology people will be commonly using fully automatic assault rifles with modern materials and cannons by 100 years.<br /> <br /> <br /> Something like 38% of the planet's land is estimated to be farmland. Yes, I suppose some wyrm plagues could make reclamation difficult.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think you're underestimating how much people could do pre-industrialization, and a good chunk of innovations were really having the idea to do something rather than dependent on technology. Say, getting to 7mm nano processors is extremely difficult, but using flintlocks rather than matchlocks? easy. Especially if we have examples rusting around to give us guidance. People are pretty resourceful and good at reverse engineering things. If we really got post apocalypted with many dangers around, I'd expect Castles and Guns to be widespread before 10 years, and something like WWII civilization before a hundred years. Some areas could be very lacking; ship building very far removed from how it's done today and how it's done today would be difficult to start doing in this new world.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair points all around. I just don\u2019t know how easy it is for some people to get started building a forge, and doing the blacksmithing. Getting the chemical requirements for the gunpowder was easy enough for medieval Koreans but then again, they had all the infrastructure of a well formed society as opposed to a total cluster fuck mess and the lack of social structure is what strikes me as most handicapping to technological development","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T13:54:01-08:00","id":1502139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1501994-running-a-werewolf-the-apocalypse-game-set-after-the-apocalypse-need-ideas?p=1502015#post1502015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My favourite whas, the wyrm suddenly has a moment of clarity, the true metis become his choosen champion and the Garou go united against the weaver instead to restore balance and the so freed Wyrm goes back to his original role of ending the sick and decaying so that the growth is not endless and so lead to a catastrophic mass decay.<br /> But on the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Apocalypse_(book)\" target=\"_blank\">wiki </a>the page has a description for every scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. I like it. That DOES sound fun","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T04:02:15-08:00","id":1502188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1501994-running-a-werewolf-the-apocalypse-game-set-after-the-apocalypse-need-ideas?p=1502138#post1502138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair points all around. I just don\u2019t know how easy it is for some people to get started building a forge, and doing the blacksmithing. Getting the chemical requirements for the gunpowder was easy enough for medieval Koreans but then again, they had all the infrastructure of a well formed society as opposed to a total cluster fuck mess and the lack of social structure is what strikes me as most handicapping to technological development</div> </div> </div> </div>I